privateData.editorialMd:
Build clamped

Read `readings` from left to right. Change each number below 0 to 0. Keep every other number as it is. Put the numbers in `clamped` in the same order.

Return the answer

Complete `stampGatesProofStrip` so it returns `clamped`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `clamped` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

